T* (You will rejoice to hear that no disaster has accompanied the) Tj
T* (commencement of an enterprise which you have regarded with such evil) Tj
T* (forebodings. I arrived here yesterday, and my first task is to assure) Tj
T* (my dear sister of my welfare and increasing confidence in the success) Tj
T* (of my undertaking.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (I am already far north of London, and as I walk in the streets of) Tj
T* (Petersburgh, I feel a cold northern breeze play upon my cheeks, which) Tj
T* (braces my nerves and fills me with delight. Do you understand this) Tj
T* (feeling? This breeze, which has travelled from the regions towards) Tj
T* (which I am advancing, gives me a foretaste of those icy climes.) Tj
T* (Inspirited by this wind of promise, my daydreams become more fervent) Tj
T* (and vivid. I try in vain to be persuaded that the pole is the seat of) Tj
T* (frost and desolation; it ever presents itself to my imagination as the) Tj
T* (region of beauty and delight. There, Margaret, the sun is for ever) Tj
T* (visible, its broad disk just skirting the horizon and diffusing a) Tj
T* (perpetual splendour. There?for with your leave, my sister, I will put) Tj
T* (some trust in preceding navigators?there snow and frost are banished;) Tj
