T* (uncontrollable passion.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (?That is also my victim!? he exclaimed. ?In his murder my) Tj
T* (crimes are consummated; the miserable series of my being is wound to its) Tj
T* (close! Oh, Frankenstein! Generous and self-devoted being! What does it) Tj
T* (avail that I now ask thee to pardon me? I, who irretrievably destroyed thee) Tj
T* (by destroying all thou lovedst. Alas! He is cold, he cannot answer) Tj
T* (me.?) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (His voice seemed suffocated, and my first impulses, which had suggested to) Tj
T* (me the duty of obeying the dying request of my friend in destroying his) Tj
T* (enemy, were now suspended by a mixture of curiosity and compassion. I) Tj
T* (approached this tremendous being; I dared not again raise my eyes to his) Tj
T* (face, there was something so scaring and unearthly in his ugliness. I) Tj
T* (attempted to speak, but the words died away on my lips. The monster) Tj
T* (continued to utter wild and incoherent self-reproaches. At length I) Tj
T* (gathered resolution to address him in a pause of the tempest of his passion.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (?Your repentance,? I said, ?is now superfluous. If you) Tj
T* (had listened to the voice of conscience and heeded the stings of remorse) Tj
T* (before you had urged your diabolical vengeance to this extremity,) Tj
T* (Frankenstein would yet have lived.?) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (?And do you dream?? said the dæmon. ?Do you think that I was then) Tj
T* (dead to agony and remorse? He,? he continued, pointing to the corpse,) Tj
T* (?he suffered not in the consummation of the deed. Oh! Not the) Tj
T* (ten-thousandth portion of the anguish that was mine during the) Tj
T* (lingering detail of its execution. A frightful selfishness hurried me) Tj
T* (on, while my heart was poisoned with remorse. Think you that the) Tj
T* (groans of Clerval were music to my ears? My heart was fashioned to be) Tj
T* (susceptible of love and sympathy, and when wrenched by misery to vice) Tj
ET
