(and hatred, it did not endure the violence of the change without) Tj
T* (torture such as you cannot even imagine.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (?After the murder of Clerval I returned to Switzerland, heart-broken) Tj
T* (and overcome. I pitied Frankenstein; my pity amounted to horror; I) Tj
T* (abhorred myself. But when I discovered that he, the author at once of) Tj
T* (my existence and of its unspeakable torments, dared to hope for) Tj
T* (happiness, that while he accumulated wretchedness and despair upon me) Tj
T* (he sought his own enjoyment in feelings and passions from the) Tj
T* (indulgence of which I was for ever barred, then impotent envy and bitter) Tj
T* (indignation filled me with an insatiable thirst for vengeance. I) Tj
T* (recollected my threat and resolved that it should be accomplished. I) Tj
T* (knew that I was preparing for myself a deadly torture, but I was the) Tj
T* (slave, not the master, of an impulse which I detested yet could not) Tj
T* (disobey. Yet when she died! Nay, then I was not miserable. I had) Tj
T* (cast off all feeling, subdued all anguish, to riot in the excess of my) Tj
T* (despair. Evil thenceforth became my good. Urged thus far, I had no) Tj
T* (choice but to adapt my nature to an element which I had willingly) Tj
T* (chosen. The completion of my demoniacal design became an insatiable) Tj
T* (passion. And now it is ended; there is my last victim!?) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (I was at first touched by the expressions of his misery; yet, when I called) Tj
T* (to mind what Frankenstein had said of his powers of eloquence and) Tj
T* (persuasion, and when I again cast my eyes on the lifeless form of my) Tj
T* (friend, indignation was rekindled within me. ?Wretch!? I said.) Tj
T* (?It is well that you come here to whine over the desolation that you) Tj
T* (have made. You throw a torch into a pile of buildings, and when they are) Tj
T* (consumed, you sit among the ruins and lament the fall. Hypocritical fiend!) Tj
T* (If he whom you mourn still lived, still would he be the object, again would) Tj
T* (he become the prey, of your accursed vengeance. It is not pity that you) Tj
T* (feel; you lament only because the victim of your malignity is withdrawn) Tj
T* (from your power.?) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (?Oh, it is not thus?not thus,? interrupted the being.) Tj
T* (?Yet such must be the impression conveyed to you by what appears to) Tj
T* (be the purport of my actions. Yet I seek not a fellow feeling in my misery.) Tj
T* (No sympathy may I ever find. When I first sought it, it was the love of) Tj
T* (virtue, the feelings of happiness and affection with which my whole being) Tj
T* (overflowed, that I wished to be participated. But now that virtue has) Tj
T* (become to me a shadow, and that happiness and affection are turned into) Tj
T* (bitter and loathing despair, in what should I seek for sympathy? I am) Tj
T* (content to suffer alone while my sufferings shall endure; when I die, I am) Tj
T* (well satisfied that abhorrence and opprobrium should load my memory. Once) Tj
T* (my fancy was soothed with dreams of virtue, of fame, and of enjoyment. Once) Tj
