(I falsely hoped to meet with beings who, pardoning my outward form, would) Tj
T* (love me for the excellent qualities which I was capable of unfolding. I was) Tj
T* (nourished with high thoughts of honour and devotion. But now crime has) Tj
T* (degraded me beneath the meanest animal. No guilt, no mischief, no) Tj
T* (malignity, no misery, can be found comparable to mine. When I run over the) Tj
T* (frightful catalogue of my sins, I cannot believe that I am the same) Tj
T* (creature whose thoughts were once filled with sublime and transcendent) Tj
T* (visions of the beauty and the majesty of goodness. But it is even so; the) Tj
T* (fallen angel becomes a malignant devil. Yet even that enemy of God and man) Tj
T* (had friends and associates in his desolation; I am alone.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (?You, who call Frankenstein your friend, seem to have a knowledge of my) Tj
T* (crimes and his misfortunes. But in the detail which he gave you of them) Tj
T* (he could not sum up the hours and months of misery which I endured) Tj
T* (wasting in impotent passions. For while I destroyed his hopes, I did) Tj
T* (not satisfy my own desires. They were for ever ardent and craving; still) Tj
T* (I desired love and fellowship, and I was still spurned. Was there no) Tj
T* (injustice in this? Am I to be thought the only criminal, when all) Tj
T* (humankind sinned against me? Why do you not hate Felix, who drove his) Tj
T* (friend from his door with contumely? Why do you not execrate the rustic) Tj
T* (who sought to destroy the saviour of his child? Nay, these are virtuous) Tj
T* (and immaculate beings! I, the miserable and the abandoned, am an) Tj
T* (abortion, to be spurned at, and kicked, and trampled on. Even now my) Tj
T* (blood boils at the recollection of this injustice.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (?But it is true that I am a wretch. I have murdered the lovely and) Tj
T* (the helpless; I have strangled the innocent as they slept and grasped to) Tj
T* (death his throat who never injured me or any other living thing. I have) Tj
T* (devoted my creator, the select specimen of all that is worthy of love and) Tj
T* (admiration among men, to misery; I have pursued him even to that) Tj
T* (irremediable ruin. There he lies, white and cold in death. You hate me, but) Tj
T* (your abhorrence cannot equal that with which I regard myself. I look on the) Tj
T* (hands which executed the deed; I think on the heart in which the) Tj
T* (imagination of it was conceived and long for the moment when these hands) Tj
T* (will meet my eyes, when that imagination will haunt my thoughts no more.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (?Fear not that I shall be the instrument of future mischief. My work) Tj
T* (is nearly complete. Neither yours nor any man?s death is needed to) Tj
T* (consummate the series of my being and accomplish that which must be done,) Tj
T* (but it requires my own. Do not think that I shall be slow to perform this) Tj
T* (sacrifice. I shall quit your vessel on the ice raft which brought me) Tj
T* (thither and shall seek the most northern extremity of the globe; I shall) Tj
T* (collect my funeral pile and consume to ashes this miserable frame, that its) Tj
T* (remains may afford no light to any curious and unhallowed wretch who would) Tj
